	(text_box "SC latch / reset / watchdog logic:\n\nU201 MCP130 generates nPOR from +3.3V.\nnPOR is used only as power-on/brownout set signal for U203A.\n\nPower-up / brownout:\nnPOR = LOW\n-> U203A nPRE = LOW\n-> Q = HIGH\n-> Q202/Q201 enable SC_Out\n-> D201 also pulls nRES LOW and keeps MCU in reset\n\nAfter nPOR release:\nnPOR = HIGH\n-> U203A keeps previous Q state\n-> MCU starts via nRES release\n\nU202 watchdog:\nnWDO = LOW on watchdog fault\n-> D203 pulls nRES LOW\n-> D207 pulls U203A nCLR LOW\n-> Q = LOW\n-> SC_Out disabled / opened\n\nLatch_SC:\nMCU can pull Latch_SC LOW\n-> D206 pulls U203A nCLR LOW\n-> Q = LOW\n-> SC_Out disabled / opened\n\nImportant:\nnPOR, nRES and nWDO are diode-isolated.\nnRES must not pull nPOR or nCLR LOW.\nThis avoids simultaneous nPRE/nCLR activation of U203A.\n\nRe-closing SC after watchdog fault or Latch_SC clear requires power-cycle / nPOR event.\nSC_State is derived from U203A Q and indicates actual latch output state."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 269.24 33.02 0)
